
## 3. How to Execute the Program

### Step 1: Clone the Repository

Clone the project repository using:

git clone https://github.com/Thahsin17/axi4-apb-adas-subsystem-source-code.git

Navigate to the repository:

cd axi4-apb-adas-subsystem-source-code

### Step 2: Install the Required Software

Install the software and Python packages listed in the `software required` file.

For the Cocotb-based verification environment, ensure that Python and Cocotb are installed.

### Step 3: Run the Cocotb Testbench

The project uses a Python-based Cocotb testbench to verify the
AXI4-to-APB communication subsystem.

The testbench is executed together with the RTL design using
an HDL simulator configured for Cocotb.

### Step 4: Verify the Simulation Results

Run the configured simulation and check the terminal output.

The testbench performs AXI4 write and read transactions and
compares the received data with the expected data.

A successful test is indicated by:

RESULT : PASS

The simulation results should show matching expected and read
data for the tested transactions.
